# Research on images

In November 2026, we split the Civica image guidance into separate pages, to help households decide when an image is worth adding to a dashboard:

- [Photography](images-photography.html)
- [Illustrations](images-illustrations.html)
- [Icons](images-icons.html)
- [Avoid images that contain text](images-text.html)
- [Alt text](images-alt-text.html)

The pages also explain how to make images as accessible as Home Assistant allows. [Accessibility](../accessibility/index.html) sets the target Civica builds to.

We want to hear whether this guidance is useful and practical in a real home. Tell us:

- how you use images to give information on your dashboards
- examples of the kinds of images you use, such as photographs, floor plans or icons
- how you create and choose your images
- how you keep images quick to load on wall panels and phones

[Give us your feedback and examples on the Civica issues page on GitHub](https://github.com/nathcymru/civica/issues).
